 # Probabilistic and Statistical Modeling
 
-Also called: PDF Transfer Functions, Bayesian Segmentation, Statistical Rendering
 
 ## Overview
-Probabilistic and Statistical Modeling methods replace hard threshold-based classification with statistical distributions or machine learning models to map volume data features to optical properties [S1, S3, unofficial]. This family addresses the ambiguity of single-voxel classification caused by the overlap of material signatures (e.g., in CT data where bone and tissue values may overlap) [S1, S3, unofficial]. Unlike standard transfer functions that assign a single opacity value, these methods assign probabilities or confidence scores, allowing for smoother transitions and more physically plausible material separation [S1, 9279-probabilistic-classification-model-for-volume-data.md, unofficial].
